        "notes": "Checked all five proof steps: closure convexity uses two finite witnesses; canonical rational enumeration avoids countable choice; nearest point exists on a compact truncation and is unique by the strict squared-norm midpoint identity. The choice-free finite-dimensional sphere supplier gives a unit limit; the limiting inequality holds for each q. Local row reduction supplies two independent normals in codimension at least two. The dimension-one relative case is included; k=0 belongs only to the separate ambient clause. All geometric terms are now explicit and the unused separation edge is removed."
