        "notes": "Checked the cone separation argument against the closed-convex separation supplier: reversing the separating functional gives the needed orientation, and conicity forces nonnegativity. Uniqueness fixes the ray of normals, since full interior excludes both signs. A finite simplex inside the strict half-space can be approximated by finitely many cone generators; barycentric continuity preserves its interior. The direct max_j a_j bound gives delta A<1 and an entire neighborhood x+tN in K. d=1 is included, and no infinite choice is used. All boundary and support notation is defined locally."
