          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Use the Darboux integral on nondegenerate intervals and the convention $\\int_a^a f=0$. Let $L\\ge0$, $T>0$, and let $f:[0,T]\\to[0,\\infty)$ be continuous. If $f(t)\\le L\\int_0^t f(s)\\,ds$ for every $t\\in[0,T]$, then $f(t)=0$ for every $t\\in[0,T]$.",
