          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Under A1–A6 of [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]], for compounds $A,B$ with $m(A)=m(B)$ and every finite spectator compound $C$, $A+C\\prec B+C$ if and only if $A\\prec B$. Consequently, for finite-support signed maps $u,v$ of equal total coefficient, define $u\\preceq_s v$ by $(v-u)^-\\prec(v-u)^+$. This relation is well-defined, agrees with $\\prec$ on nonnegative maps, is invariant under adding a common signed map, is transitive, and is closed under addition of two comparisons. No comparison hypothesis is used.",
