      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "Checked all four steps and the corrected local geometric suppliers. Empty ambient interior forces affine dimension below d via the relative-interior simplex. Codimension at least two contradicts unique support. In codimension one, the strict-successor sector shares the hull; its last segment point is a relative boundary point because the chart is open and the sector relatively closed. Its in-hull support extends to an ambient plane distinct from the hull, contradicting S2. The d=1 interval argument and zero-dimensional hull exclusion are explicit; only finitely many witnesses are selected."
