          "case": "one",
          "status": "not_applicable",
          "reason": "Under [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]], the sectors are nested: if $y\\in A_x$, then $A_y\\subseteq A_x$; equality holds when $y\\in\\partial A_x$, and $A_y\\subset\\operatorname{int}_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$ when $y\\in\\operatorname{int}_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$. Boundary one: The item makes no one boundary claim; this case does not apply to its stated result.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Under [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]], the sectors are nested: if $y\\in A_x$, then $A_y\\subseteq A_x$; equality holds when $y\\in\\partial A_x$, and $A_y\\subset\\operatorname{int}_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$ when $y\\in\\operatorname{int}_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$. For every $x,y\\in\\Gamma_i$, either $x\\prec y$ or $y\\prec x$ (possibly both). Strict comparison is exactly interior membership: $x\\prec\\prec y$ if and only if $y\\in\\operatorname{int}_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "b37f9875c8f43e129fb7eb8c05b78d27b885a1db44df1d2d5cc1f0fd96ff27e4",
            "scope_only_not_proof_acceptance": true
          }
        },
