            "source_excerpt": "Under [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]], each simple domain has one orientation sign $\\varepsilon_i\\in\\{-1,1\\}$, constant across the domain, such that at fixed work coordinate $v$, $x\\prec y$ exactly when $\\varepsilon_i(u_y-u_x)\\ge0$. In coordinates oriented so $\\varepsilon_i=1$, for each $x\\in\\Gamma_i$ the projection $\\rho_x$ of $\\partial_{\\Gamma_i}A_x$ onto work coordinates is open and connected; the boundary is the graph $(u_x(v),v)$ of a $C^1$ function with locally Lipschitz derivative\n\n$$Du_x(v)=-P_i(u_x(v),v).$$\n\nIf $y\\in\\partial A_x$, then $A_y=A_x$ and their boundary graphs agree.",
