        "notes": "Reviewed all nine steps, with global closedness supplied by a local closed-ball truncation. Supports agree locally/globally by convexity, and supports of A_x at z must equal the unique support of A_z. Moved local constancy after the fixed-fiber orientation deduction so that neighboring boundary fibers transfer their sign to all their states without a forward premise. The nested compact-interval recursion gives a unique interior-domain limit, contradicting the inward ray. Graph solutions use a local Lipschitz estimate and the repaired zero-start integral inequality; convex graph secant/support bounds prove total differentiability with locally Lipschitz derivative. Relative closure and connected projections propagate graph equality to equal sectors. The integral t=0 convention is compatible; no change to the stated result."
