        "notes": "All six steps checked. T4 strips are open by sector nesting and cover the domain. An overlap contains a strict vertical pair; reference coordinates increase, and signed subtraction supplies a positive affine transition. Finite segment paths give compact connected sets and a finite connected strip subcover, so a rooted tree glues all finite target states. Reversible scaled-tag transport retains effective coefficients alpha_j r_j; equal bookkeeping mass gives equal total effective amount. Signed reference differences compare by their scalar coefficient, including zero total mass where both maps are empty. Infinite choice and entropy across different compositions are not used."
