            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\Gamma\\subset\\mathbb R^{n+1}$ be a simple domain satisfying the forward-sector hypotheses and T1–T4. Let $S$ be the additive extensive entropy supplied by [[thm-tdmath-additive-entropy-representation]] after CH for its finite scaled products is proved by [[thm-tdmath-reference-strip-gluing]]. Then either all pairs of states in $\\Gamma$ are thermally equivalent, or there are $x,y$ on one entropy level (equivalently, one adiabat $\\partial A_x$ by [[thm-tdmath-sector-nesting]]) with $x\\not\\sim_T y$.",
