      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "All seven steps checked. CH applies after the fixed positive type-weight normalization; entropy concavity follows A7, and finite concave functions are continuous by the repaired supplier. Energy one-sided slopes exist by monotone secants, are finite by neighboring secants, and are strictly positive by strict increase. T1/T2 and the same-type entropy representation identify thermal equilibrium with intersecting reciprocal slope intervals. Finite interval intersection plus compactness gives a common class interval. Under the negated second alternative, levels belong to single classes; energy-fiber ranges are open intervals and finite overlapping covers order the global level-to-class map. T4 forces each class range open in a connected entropy range, hence one class. No empirical inference is asserted; producer finding reader:6:15 is false-positive as shown by exact common signed translation."
