          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "Statement selects two nonempty simple charts satisfying the forward-sector premises. Its later composition comparison includes the zero-total empty compound by reflexivity, as the proof final comparison branch states.",
          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let $\\Gamma_1,\\Gamma_2$ be simple domains in a family of finite thermal joins satisfying A1–A7, S1–S3, T1–T5, and C1 of [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]] and [[def-tdmath-thermal-contact-hypotheses]]. Then there are $x_0\\prec\\prec x_1$ in $\\Gamma_1$ and $y_0\\prec\\prec y_1$ in $\\Gamma_2$ such that\n\n$$(x_0,y_1)\\sim(x_1,y_0).$$\n\nMoreover, for every fixed finite composition of scaled copies of $\\Gamma_1$ and $\\Gamma_2$, any two equal-mass states of that same composition are comparable (CH). The conclusion is conditional on the explicitly stated join-coherence and universal-range assumptions C1 and T5.",
