      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "All four steps checked. Explicit AC chooses simultaneous reference states, entropy representatives and nonempty calibrator tuples over I; finite choices within each later comparison add no further choice premise. Positive entropy gaps define mu_i/Delta_i>0, including the meter branch with both gaps one. Finite tagged factorization makes the sum additive and extensive. Signed reductions have zero total coefficient and zero same-type entropy; calibrators replace type increments by finite meter increments. Equal fixed composition cancels base maps; meter positive/negative parts have equal mass, and its entropy representation proves both directions. Changing type origins contributes conserved amount-weighted offsets only. No infinite sums or cross-composition conclusion is made."
