        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "Reviewed the full definition and all cost consumers. Products must be actual sums in the product state set; surjectivity supplies endpoint factorization, and positive scaling is a bijection onto the scaled state set. Empty type is the zero map, not an untyped symbol. The scalar mass and primitive amount conditions remain separate. Defined ordered extended reals, partial sums, scaling, negation and greatest-lower-bound convention; empty and unbounded-below witness sets retain +infinity and -infinity. Finite entropy and same-composition representation are adopted from the calibrated family with its AC hypothesis. These explicit closure assumptions make every spectator, scaling and chain endpoint construction admissible."
