      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "All five proof steps checked with the repaired state closure. Summing a closed chain inputs/outputs gives equal composition and nonnegative entropy difference. Product costs use finite common spectators admitted by the product maps; chains allow independent input/output states at intermediate types, so no false state-matching condition is introduced. Fixed-catalyst padding is cost-preserving, and scaling with its inverse gives equality of finite and infinite infima. Triangle and product inequalities cover finite, unbounded-below and +infinity cases while excluding undefined opposite infinities. Finite reverse witnesses bound all forward witnesses below. The new product closure resolves the originally undefined witness in step 1.2."
