      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-6",
        "notes": "All six proof steps checked. No-sinks plus finite reverse witness excludes -infinity. If pair classes agree, zero-cost equivalence with catalyst bounds F(P,D) in both directions; common-catalyst invariance identifies the original two costs, so p is representative-independent even at +infinity. Homogeneity and product subadditivity make p sublinear, and no-sinks makes its finite domain symmetric. The exact infinite-valued sandwich supplier first applies real Hahn–Banach on that finite domain and then extends by a basis under AC, yielding the two-sided offset bounds. Admitted transitions necessarily have equal mass, so the repaired iff theorem applies. The final subtraction is between finite real quantities for any admitted transition. No strict/no-gap extension is inferred."
