          "case_scope": {
            "source_section": "Statement",
            "source_excerpt": "Let a family of simple domains satisfy [[def-tdmath-forward-sector-hypotheses]], and suppose every pair has an admitted simple thermal join satisfying T1 and T2 of [[def-tdmath-thermal-contact-hypotheses]]. Then the fixed-work orientation signs from [[thm-tdmath-forward-boundary-graph]] agree throughout the family. One common affine proof-coordinate convention $u'=\\varepsilon u$, $\\varepsilon\\in\\{-1,1\\}$, therefore makes each fixed-work accessibility order increase with $u'$ and preserves the energy-sum formula for joins. This is a mathematical coordinate convention; it does not change a physical energy quantity or assert a sign of a measured temperature.",
            "current_raw_sha256": "b5530da2ba1c0eaf9cfe0f86a10e545ca855f4c1b67691ee1e017c6f43c0642e",
